	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/prism/path_tracing/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Quality: a bounce of light traced at every pixel. Performance: the bounced light read from the lightmaps, a bounce traced for the characters and vehicles alone; faster."/>
		<string text="PRISM: the traced light smoothed over the frames before and the pixels about. DLSS RR: NVIDIA DLSS Ray Reconstruction (offered once installed), which also brings the view to the screen's resolution; from the next start. Off: the light as traced, grainy (for checking).|DLSS's plugin: the prism-plugins README."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Enhanced: plasma bolts and needles light their surroundings too, each with a glow, and a muzzle flash lights your own weapon. Classic: only the lights the Xbox had.|Classic for everyone in a Pro 2v2 game; yours again after it."/>
		<string text="How bright plasma, needles, grenades, blasts and shield flares light their surroundings. Full: as bright as the game's own colours; white lights such as the flashlight keep their light."/>
		<string text="How deep the colour of the light they cast is. Pure: the game's own colours, plasma green and needle pink; Pale: nearer white, as a real glow's light is."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="The objects' shapes traced. As Drawn: the remodels as drawn, within 40 units. Game's: the game's own models, cheaper."/>
		<string text="Keeps each object's traced shape from frame to frame, refitting only what moved: much less work."/>
		<string text="The moving objects' leaves, fences and grates cast shadows through their holes. The level's are in the lightmaps."/>
	</strings>
